        "id": 1892347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-29T18:29:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "CONFIG_FINEIBT is not something you can change. It\u0027s a computed value that represents whether the kernel has the *capability* to use FineIBT. Whether FineIBT is used depends on the `cfi\u003d` kernel command-line parameter, and setting `cfi\u003dfineibt` enables FineIBT via code patching on boot.\n\nWhat `CONFIG_CFI_AUTO_DEFAULT` does is that it changes the default value of the `cfi\u003d` kcmdline parameter so that it uses `cfi\u003dfineibt` when the hardware has support for IBT.\n\nThis should all go in the commit message, of course.",
      "parentUuid": "535f9a87_371a0483",
      "revId": "f4db7b417d7e3ecba53975a913ceeeaf1f10882d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
